# Sparse-checkout list for a server or LXC. install.sh copies this into
# .git/info/sparse-checkout and appends one !line per git-crypt path in
# .gitattributes, so newly encrypted files exclude themselves.
#
# Everything not listed here is checked out. Mac-only clutter is left alone on
# purpose: a wezterm config on a box with no wezterm is inert, and keeping the
# list short is worth more than keeping $HOME tidy. Only things that actually
# break belong here.
/*

# The workstation shell layer. Not harmful, but this is the layer boundary.
!/.config/zsh/rc.work.d/

# The workstation half of the mise tool list. conf.d/server.toml is the other
# half and stays; exclude.workstation drops that one instead.
!/.config/mise/conf.d/work.toml

# Pulled in by .config/git/config through a relative include. It turns on
# commit and tag signing with an ssh key held in 1Password, so every commit on
# a box without that agent fails with "Couldn't get agent socket?", and it
# rewrites https github URLs to ssh, so clones fail too.
!/.config/git/config.work

# The git-crypt key, itself encrypted to a GPG key that is not here. Useless
# without it, but there is no reason to put it on eight machines.
!/.git-crypt/
